@startuml 17_act_requirement_flow
!include _style.iuml
title Requirement: built by allowlist at the node, validated by strict schema at the hub (not signed)

' declare swimlanes in reading order
|Purchaser client|
|Hospital node|
|Supplier hub|
|Purchaser client|
start
:POST /articles/{id}/requirement\n{answered_question_ids?};
|Hospital node|
:Authorize node user (PURCHASER);
if (Per-user count above\nREQUIREMENT_RATE_LIMIT_PER_HOUR?) then (yes)
  :429; write alert RATE_EXCEEDED;
  stop
else (no)
endif
:Read article_projection ONLY\n(never the article row: name, internal id,\nprice, quantities, raw are unreachable);
:Keep template attributes with shareable = true;
:Move EGRESS_DENY_ATTRIBUTES\nto withheld_attributes;
:Free text only as synonym code\nor short text (<= 60 chars), else unknown;
:Map sources to coarse origins\n(MASTER, EXTRACTED, REFERENCE, PURCHASER);
if (SHARE_PRODUCT_HINTS?) then (yes)
  :Add product_hints: brand,\nmanufacturer article no.,\nGTIN only if check digit valid;
else (no, default)
  :product_hints = null;
endif
:Validate RequirementPayload\n(extra keys fail);
:Insert egress_log (kind REQUIREMENT,\ncontent, sha256, user) BEFORE returning;\nalert at 80% of the limit;
|Purchaser client|
:Show the requirement JSON\n("what leaves the hospital");
:POST to hub: /search, /assessments\nor /assessments/{id}/requirements\n(hub token);
|Supplier hub|
:Hub token -> principal + tenant\n(tenant never taken from the body);
if (RequirementPayload valid\n(no unknown fields)?) then (no)
  :422;
  stop
else (yes)
endif
if (requirement_version supported and\ntemplate_code known?) then (no)
  :422;
  stop
else (yes)
endif
:requirement_hash = core record_hash\n(attributes + unknown / unavailable / withheld);
if (Endpoint?) then (search)
  :Use for candidate search; discard\n(only tenant, time, counts\nin short-retention access log);
else (assessment)
  :Store in requirements\n(payload + requirement_hash);
  :Attach to assessment\n(current_requirement_id; mark answered\nPURCHASER questions);
endif
stop

note right
  Why not signed (D34): the client already
  receives all article data from the node, and
  the hub schema enforces minimization. A node
  signature could be added later around the same
  payload (typ requirement+jwt, about 1/2 day).
end note

@enduml
